{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411786-what-do-you-think-of-scion-2e-combining-all-the-different-myths-into-one-world","id":1411786,"title":"What do you think of Scion 2e combining all the different myths into one World?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-09-04T07:06:05-07:00","id":1411786,"title":"What do you think of Scion 2e combining all the different myths into one World?","content":"I haven\u2019t read Titanomachy yet but I probably will over the weekend.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T07:08:47-07:00","id":1411787,"title":"","content":"I plan to run it as such that each Pantheon has it's own Realms - as kind of 'super Terra Incognita' - and they just 'cross' on the Earth. You can have Nine Worlds, all the Indra States, Duat and all the Olympians Realms in the same place - they just have different portals to get there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T07:15:36-07:00","id":1411791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411786-what-do-you-think-of-scion-2e-combining-all-the-different-myths-into-one-world#post1411786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you think of Scion 2e combining all the different myths into one World?</div> </div> </div> </div>Worked pretty well for the real world already, so why not? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10624-sacerdos","name":"Sacerdos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10624_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"231"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T07:31:27-07:00","id":1411797,"title":"","content":"My way to see the world is basically it\u2019s the natural world as we know it.<br /> <br /> Terrae Incognitae are a bit tricky, most of them you need to know how to get into or have some divine interaction to get there by mistake. For example, to go to Alfheim you need to know how to climb Yggdrasil, and to do that you need get to some special places or a help from a god to reach it, while to get to Arcadia (the mythical one, not the region in Greece) you need to be in the right area and \u201cget lost\u201d in the right way.<br /> <br /> The god realms are another thing, they are not Terrae Incognitae, even when they have a physical location in the world (Mount Olympus) or in the cosmology (Asgaard), you need to get to the right place AND do some trick that only gods and maybe a demigod with the proper purview can do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T10:29:52-07:00","id":1411827,"title":"","content":"I'm going fucking bonkers with it. Myth is fucking bonkers. Embrace it. Yeah, there's hundreds of Gods that claim to be moving the sun. They're all right, from a certain point of view. Don't worry too much about it.<br /> <br /> For most lay people, the World is much like our world. The thing to keep in mind is that like... Through the VAST majority of human history, the myths and legends and religions were known to be true. Ask the people of Hellenic Greece about Centaurs, they'd go &quot;Yeah, centaurs exist. They're like, over there-&quot; and gesture Off That-a-Way. They exist, everyone knows it, it's just kind of accepted.<br /> <br /> And I am very much including the present in this. Like, ask any of the religious people today if they doubt their religions.<br /> <br /> You'll probably get more answers than the number of people you ask. In the World of Scion, it's all true, at once. Athena at some point <i>may</i> have been a Hero who eventually achieved Apotheosis, but <i>now</i> she is a Goddess, and Always Has Been, because Fate and her Legend declare it so. Truth is mutable, the World runs on Story-Around-The-Campfire Logic (which is even more fluid than Action Movie Logic), go wild.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":2142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","user":"Kyman201","date":". 09-04-2020, 01:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T10:36:55-07:00","id":1411832,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10624-sacerdos\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar10624_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"10624\" data-vbnamecard=\"10624\">Sacerdos</a> I Liked your post.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2142_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2142\" data-vbnamecard=\"2142\">Kyman201</a> In Mythic Denizens there\u2019s a nation of centaurs in eastern Montana.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T11:23:44-07:00","id":1411840,"title":"","content":"Thanks, Penelope, but totally not my point. My main point is frankly something that Sacerdos put better.<br /> <br /> &quot;[All religions being true] worked pretty well for the Real World already&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T12:04:01-07:00","id":1411847,"title":"","content":"I meant that stuff like a bunch of centaurs living in Montana is one of the major differences between our world and the World. But in the World we objectively KNOW (can\u2019t find the italics button) that all religions are true; irl that may or may not be true.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T17:41:19-07:00","id":1411960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411786-what-do-you-think-of-scion-2e-combining-all-the-different-myths-into-one-world?p=1411827#post1411827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm going fucking bonkers with it. Myth is fucking bonkers. Embrace it. Yeah, there's hundreds of Gods that claim to be moving the sun. They're all right, from a certain point of view. Don't worry too much about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like to think that, from a Divine perspective, The World is like a gemstone with infinite facets, and sometimes what's going on at that particular place and time - such as what the Sun is and how it works - depends on just how you are looking at it at that moment. And, just from personal interpretation, I'm guessing that the more interaction Heroes (and Demigods and Gods) have with other Pantheons, the more facets they can start to wrap their head around. At least that's my tentative read on the subject. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T23:59:36-07:00","id":1412015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411786-what-do-you-think-of-scion-2e-combining-all-the-different-myths-into-one-world?p=1411960#post1411960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I like to think that, from a Divine perspective, The World is like a gemstone with infinite facets, and sometimes what's going on at that particular place and time - such as what the Sun is and how it works - depends on just how you are looking at it at that moment. And, just from personal interpretation, I'm guessing that the more interaction Heroes (and Demigods and Gods) have with other Pantheons, the more facets they can start to wrap their head around. At least that's my tentative read on the subject.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I wager that things become more apparent as your Legend goes up. If you're in the company of Zeus on the World itself, probably safe to assume that you're heavily favoring Theoi Rules at the moment.<br /> <br /> (Within reason. If you're a Scion of Zeus, even if you're in the halls of an Aesir, probably a good idea to still follow the Greek laws of Hospitality. If you break THOSE, you may get vaporized on the spot, <i>if you're lucky</i>)<br /> <br /> Edit: Also, if you're deliberately pulling things from Outside Context <i>in</i>, then I think there may be a part of Demigod that will talk about those kinds of things. Neall mentioned it in a podcast: Like the moment in the Dad of Boy game where Kratos is told that no flame of mortal world nor of Asgard will burn within this one realm... And Kratos just pulls out his Blades of Chaos, which come from outside the setup, and thus are immune to the &quot;No flame may burn&quot; rule.<br /> <br /> So yeah... :P Go nuts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":2142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","user":"Kyman201","date":". 09-05-2020, 03:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T02:48:27-07:00","id":1412029,"title":"","content":"I still have trouble wrapping my head around the \u201cAll myths are true\u201d concept, but your explanations help a lot <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2142_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2142\" data-vbnamecard=\"2142\">Kyman201</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12890_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12890\" data-vbnamecard=\"12890\">No One of Consequence</a>. Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T03:24:22-07:00","id":1412037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1411786-what-do-you-think-of-scion-2e-combining-all-the-different-myths-into-one-world?p=1412029#post1412029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still have trouble wrapping my head around the \u201cAll myths are true\u201d concept, but your explanations help a lot <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2142_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2142\" data-vbnamecard=\"2142\">Kyman201</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12890_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12890\" data-vbnamecard=\"12890\">No One of Consequence</a>. Thanks.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm going from personal agnostic point of view, but to me - the World as setting is 'just' our material world. Gods and Myths are only extra layeres to it. More, each Panthons is like 'special frequency' in the greater World setting. If you take out all Pantheons and all Myths - the World will just works as real life Earth. It's simple as that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}